  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPPF Core Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to IPPF. IPPF&#x2019;s new strategy (2023-2028) aims to strengthen gender-transformative initiatives and protect and promote SRHR for all, especially women, girls, and young people in all their diversities, with priority of vulnerable and marginalized groups, and those left furthest behind. Providing quality, rights-based and gender-sensitive SRHR services and information is at the heart of IPPFs strategy.
 
IPPF&#x2019;s overall impact goal is to ensure that &#x201c;all people are free to make choices about their sexuality and well-being, in a world without discrimination&#x201d;. To achieve this, IPPF&#x2019;s ToC presents four outcomes: 
1) Quality person-centered care to more people, in more places
2) Societal and legislative change for universal SRH
3) Amplify impact by building bridges, shaping discourse, and connecting communities, movements, and sectors
4) Replenish and nurture the Federation from a common value base and unleash our collective power for greater impact. 

SRHR, safe abortion, Comprehencive sexuality education (CSE), Family planning, FGM, SGBV, work with boys and men on positiv maskulinities.

A total of 140 countries are involved, including Norwegian partner countries: Afghanistan, Colombia, Ethiopia, Indonesia, Mozambique, Palestine, Somalia, South Sudan, Syria and Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
